<h1>FillHoles</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> Reconstructs missing data (holes) in selected mesh areas.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Parameters</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">Method</i></b>  sets filling method. Available options are: <i>FlatFill</i>  for flat filling method and <i>CrvBased</i>  for curvature based filling method.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">LimitEdges</i></b>  restricts the number of filled holes by the number of their boundary edges. Available options are <i>Yes</i> and <i>No</i>.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">MaxEdges</i></b>  number of edges for filling restriction.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>UI Commands</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><i style="font-style:italic;">Mesh &gt; Fill</i> from the main menu. <i style="font-style:italic;">Tools &gt; Fill</i> from the tree context menu for meshes. <b style="font-weight:bold;">Ctrl + F</b> shortcut.</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Examples:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="font-family:Courier New;">FillHoles( Method="FlatFill", LimitEdges=Yes, MaxEdges=50 )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode"><font style="font-family:Courier New;" face="Courier New">FillHoles( Method="CrvBased", LimitEdges=No, MaxEdges=1000000 )</font></p>
